<title>FRANCE: France halts Swiss beef imports.</title>
<headline>France halts Swiss beef imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>France on Friday suspended imports of live cattle and beef from Switzerland, the European country most affected by mad cow disease after Britain, Agriculture Minister Philippe Vasseur told a news conference.  </p>
<p>&quot;This precautionary measure is taken pending the official position of the European Union,&quot; Vasseur said.</p>
<p>&quot;It is justified by the absolute priority we place on protecting consumers,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Switzerland plans to spend some 6.5 million Swiss francs ($4.90 million) to slaughter at least 1,500 cows to eradicate mad cow disease.</p>
<p>Switzerland has reported 230 cases of Bovine Spongiform Encephalopathy (BSE), the most of any country except Britain. Scientists suspect tainted beef products can trigger the brain-wasting Creuzfeldt-Jakob Disease in humans.</p>
</text>
